[190.432,"o","── PLAN · nothing below has run ───────────────────────────────────────\r\nThis is what will be deleted from your DigitalOcean account:\r\n\r\n  # Everything the Terraform state in .openvidu/digitalocean holds: the master Droplet,\r\n  # the media node Droplets, the VPC, the firewalls, the tags, the autoscaler's Function\r\n  # (its namespace and its trigger) and the media nodes it created, the SSH key, the\r\n  # Spaces key, the Space with the recordings and Meet data. A Space must be empty to go,\r\n  # and the master writes into it until it is gone, so the Spaces are emptied between two\r\n  # passes; only a Space the state holds is emptied, never one of your own (SpaceName).\r\n  # The media nodes the autoscaler created are not in the state: the template's destroy\r\n  # deletes them by their tags, with the API token in DIGITALOCEAN_TOKEN.\r\n  # OPENVIDU_STACK_DESTROY=1 tells it the whole stack goes, so no media node drains first.\r\n  terraform -chdir=.openvidu/digitalocean init -input=false -no-color -force-copy\r\n  env OPENVIDU_STACK_DESTROY=1 terraform -chdir=.openvidu/digitalocean destroy -auto-approve -input=false -no-color\r\n  env AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=*** AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=*** AWS_SESSION_TOKEN= aws s3 rm s3://openvidu-e2e-do-el-a102129-space-b2f8c59132 --recursive --endpoint-url https://fra1.digitaloceanspaces.com\r\n  env OPENVIDU_STACK_DESTROY=1 terraform -chdir=.openvidu/digitalocean destroy -auto-approve -input=false -no-color\r\n\r\n--delete-data: the recordings and Meet data are in the Space: this deletes them.\r\n── end of plan ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n\r\n"]
